---
/**
 * Memberships — the retention lever. 41% of venues have no membership page at
 * all (playbook-sim-venue.md §4). Ported to the converged Paper design
 * 2026-08-03 (FW-3967); spec in `design/SUBPAGE-EXPLORATION.md`.
 *
 * **The idea: two unlike products get two grammars.** Monthly is a card
 * comparison. LinksFlex is a `FuelGauge` — bank sizes across, tiers down, a
 * proportional bar per cell — because an hour bank is a punch card, not a SaaS
 * plan. Drawing both as pricing cards is what made this page read as four
 * near-identical boxes, and it also flattered the wrong product: a bank of hours
 * compared card-to-card against a subscription looks like a worse subscription.
 *
 * **Two honest things this page keeps, both of which cost us a sale sometimes:**
 *
 * 1. *The recommendation is arithmetic.* Individual is flagged "Start here if
 *    you are not sure" because $149 ÷ $35 pays back after about 4¼ hours of bay
 *    time a month — a reason the customer can check, not a "Most popular"
 *    sticker, which is a claim about other people that we have no data for.
 * 2. *The chooser's last row is "neither".* Play now and then, and the right
 *    answer is to book a bay at $35 and buy nothing. A page willing to tell you
 *    not to buy is more persuasive than one that isn't.
 *
 * Prices are HTML text (playbook-core.md §8). On the current live site every one
 * of these numbers is inside a JPEG. They now live in the `memberships`
 * collection as NUMBERS, so the per-hour figures are divided rather than stored
 * and cannot drift out of agreement with the prices beside them.
 *
 * ⚠️ "Hours never expire" is the CLIENT'S marketing line and it is true as far
 * as it goes, but the LinksFlex T&Cs attach a condition: hours stay valid "for
 * as long as the customer is in good standing with the Company and the Company
 * continues to offer the associated service". This page states that condition
 * once, in "Before you join", and every other mention points at it. Do not
 * restore a bare "never expire" — a promise published without its condition is
 * the shape of a complaint (truth-audit §U5).
 *
 * ✅ The guest policy is RESOLVED (client-answers.md §13): members bring guests,
 * there is no guest fee, and the member must be present. It carried a
 * `PendingTag` because the client's own price card said "only available for the
 * package purchaser" and "No Guest Fees" in the same breath. We were right not
 * to guess — an earlier draft had answered it in the customer's favour without
 * saying so, and this is the one that costs somebody money at the till
 * (truth-audit §U3) — but the answer is now known, so it is stated plainly.
 *
 * ⚠️ LinksFlex "Anytime" is still held back, but OUR REASONING WAS WRONG and is
 * recorded here so nobody reinstates it. We withheld it because at $39.56–$45.75
 * an hour it costs more than the $35 walk-up rate, and we read that as a pricing
 * mistake (strategy.md §7.4). It is not: Anytime is an IN-SEASON promo and is
 * priced for in-season demand, while Summer Monthly is the summer answer
 * (client-answers.md §13). Publishing it is now a positioning question — does it
 * read as a premium or as a worse deal — not a repricing one. Decide before
 * launch rather than leaving it in a `StubNote` by default.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/venue/SectionHead.astro';
import HeroStrip from '../components/venue/HeroStrip.astro';
import FuelGauge from '../components/venue/FuelGauge.astro';
import ReadoutCell from '../components/venue/ReadoutCell.astro';
import GapCell from '../components/venue/GapCell.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import { buttonClasses } from '../lib/buttons';
import { globalData } from '../data/global';

/** The walk-up rate every membership on this page is measured against. */
const WALK_UP = 35;

/**
 * The early-bird deadline, as one date in one place. ISO so the inline
 * script can parse it; the label beside it is what a reader sees.
 */
const EARLY_BIRD_ENDS = '2026-10-31';
const EARLY_BIRD_LABEL = '31 October 2026';
const earlyBirdLive = new Date() <= new Date(EARLY_BIRD_ENDS + 'T23:59:59');

const all = (await getCollection('memberships'))
  .filter((m) => m.data.published)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

const monthly = all.filter((m) => m.data.kind === 'monthly');
const flex = all.filter((m) => m.data.kind === 'flex');

/**
 * The strip's LinksFlex headline: the best per-hour rate a general reader can
 * ACTUALLY BUY, so age-restricted tiers are excluded from it.
 *
 * The Junior bank is the cheapest per hour on the page by a distance, and a
 * "LinksFlex from $20.81" headline computed over every tier is arithmetic that
 * is technically correct and still misleads — an adult reads a price and then
 * discovers they are not eligible. `ageRestricted` exists for this one line.
 */
const bestPerHour = Math.min(
  ...flex.filter((f) => !f.data.ageRestricted).flatMap((f) => f.data.banks.map((b) => b.price / b.hours)),
);
/**
 * The cheapest monthly a GENERAL READER can actually buy.
 *
 * `ageRestricted` now guards the monthly tiers as well as the flex ones, and for
 * the same reason it was invented: Senior / Vet and Junior are both $149, both
 * cheaper than anything an unrestricted adult can join, and a "Monthly from
 * $149" headline computed over every tier is arithmetic that is correct and
 * still misleads. The general entry point is Off-Peak at $199.
 *
 * (Vet is a service status rather than an age. The field is doing the job it was
 * built for — keeping a headline to prices the reader can act on — so it guards
 * that tier too rather than growing a second flag that means the same thing.)
 */
const generalMonthly = monthly.filter((m) => !m.data.ageRestricted);
const cheapestMonthly = Math.min(...generalMonthly.map((m) => m.data.price ?? Infinity));

/**
 * The payback point for a given tier, divided rather than asserted.
 *
 * ⚠️ THIS TAKES A TIER. It used to be one number computed from the cheapest
 * monthly and then printed inside every recommended card — which was right only
 * while the cheapest tier and the recommended tier were the same one. They are
 * no longer: the recommendation is Anytime at $299 and the cheapest general tier
 * is Off-Peak at $199, so a single shared figure would have printed "$299 ÷ $35
 * pays for itself past about 5.7 hours", which is the wrong quotient beside the
 * right division. Divide per tier or do not print the sentence.
 *
 * One decimal: the exact quotient is false precision in a sentence that already
 * says "about", and the division is printed beside it either way.
 */
const paybackFor = (price: number) => (price / WALK_UP).toFixed(1);
const payback = paybackFor(cheapestMonthly);

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Golf Memberships & LinksFlex — Lakeville & Stillwater',
  metaDescription:
    'Monthly memberships and LinksFlex prepaid hours at The Links, Lakeville and Stillwater MN. No expiry date on LinksFlex hours. Compare tiers and join online.',
};

/**
 * The chooser. Its last row is the point of it — see the file header. Ordered by
 * how often the answer applies, so the reader meets themselves early.
 */
const chooser = [
  {
    when: 'You play most weeks',
    answer: 'Monthly membership',
    why: `Two hours a day and the 21-day booking window. It pays for itself past about ${payback} hours a month.`,
  },
  {
    when: 'You play in bursts',
    answer: 'LinksFlex hours',
    why: 'A bank you draw down whenever, with no monthly bill and no expiry date. A quiet month costs you nothing.',
  },
  {
    when: 'You play now and then',
    answer: 'Neither',
    why: `Book a bay at $${WALK_UP} an hour and buy nothing. Up to six of you, same price. Come back to this page when that stops being the cheapest way.`,
    none: true,
  },
];

/** The six questions the playbook says a membership page must answer. */
const smallPrint = [
  [
    'What you get',
    'Bay time, not lessons or league entry. Leagues and instruction are booked and paid for separately.',
  ],
  [
    'Hours restrictions',
    'The monthly memberships include two hours a day and are subject to opening hours — a membership does not guarantee a walk-in bay. Every tier except Anytime is limited to the window printed on it, and the LinksFlex hours the same; there is no restriction on how long you take to use a bank.',
  ],
  ['Do you have to be there?', 'Yes. The member has to be present at the tee time.'],
  [
    'Extra hours',
    'Once you have used the two hours a day your membership includes, anything beyond that is charged at the normal rate — unless a specific package says otherwise.',
  ],
  [
    'Commitment',
    'The monthly memberships bill automatically each month until you cancel. LinksFlex is a one-off purchase with no monthly commitment. Its hours have no expiry date — the terms hold them open for as long as you are in good standing and we still offer the service — but they are non-transferable and all sales are final.',
  ],
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {
    /* 1. HERO + the 4-cell strip. The strip answers the four things a visitor
      screens on before reading a word of the page: what the two products cost at
      their entry point, what the best hourly rate is, and what it costs to buy
      nothing — which is the number everything else is compared against. */
  }
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter pt-s8 pb-s7 lg:px-gutter-lg lg:pt-s9 lg:pb-s8">
      <p class="caps-label text-amber">Two ways to pay less per hour</p>
      <h1 class="mt-s5 text-hero leading-hero font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-white">Memberships</h1>
      <p class="mt-s5 max-w-prose-page border-l-slab border-amber pl-s4 text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        A monthly membership if you play most weeks, or a bank of prepaid LinksFlex hours with no expiry date if you
        play in bursts. You do not need to be any good at golf to be worth one.
      </p>

      <HeroStrip
        class="mt-s8"
        tone="dark"
        cells={[
          { label: 'Monthly from', value: `$${cheapestMonthly}`, qualifier: 'a month, both venues' },
          { label: 'LinksFlex from', value: `$${bestPerHour.toFixed(2)}`, qualifier: 'an hour, both venues' },
          { label: 'Walk up', value: `$${WALK_UP}`, qualifier: 'an hour, no membership at all' },
          { label: 'Season', value: '2026/27', qualifier: 'the prices on this page' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /*
     * EARLY BIRD — A DATED PROMOTION, AND IT HAS TO BE ABLE TO EXPIRE.
     *
     * A discount band that outlives its own deadline is the defect this repo has
     * shipped before: content that was true when written, still on the page a
     * year later. This one cannot, because it retires itself twice over.
     *
     *   1. `EARLY_BIRD_ENDS` is checked at BUILD time, so any deploy after the
     *      date drops the band from the HTML.
     *   2. The inline script re-checks against the VISITOR's clock, because a
     *      static site that nobody rebuilds keeps serving whatever it last
     *      built. Without this, no deploy between now and November means a
     *      November visitor is told the offer ends on 31 October.
     *
     * The date is also written into the band in words, so even a stale render is
     * self-evidently expired rather than quietly wrong.
     *
     * Ember band, paper ink — the same treatment as the league waitlist, and the
     * only other place on this page allowed to carry the action colour.
     */
  }
  {
    earlyBirdLive && (
      <section class="on-accent-band bg-primary" data-early-bird data-ends={EARLY_BIRD_ENDS}>
        <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-content flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-s6 gap-y-s3 px-gutter py-s6 lg:px-gutter-lg">
          <p class="caps-label text-label-sm text-surface">Early bird</p>
          <p class="text-lead leading-body font-bold text-surface">20% off memberships · 10% off hour packages</p>
          <p class="text-body leading-body text-surface">
            Ends {EARLY_BIRD_LABEL}. Gift cards cannot be used to pay for a membership.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var band = document.querySelector('[data-early-bird]');
      if (!band) return;
      // Ends at the close of the stated day, in the visitor's own timezone.
      var ends = new Date(band.dataset.ends + 'T23:59:59');
      if (!isNaN(ends.valueOf()) && Date.now() > ends.valueOf()) band.hidden = true;
    })();
  </script>

  {/* 2. THE CHOOSER. Three rows, and the third one sells nothing. */}
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={1}>Which one, if either</SectionHead>
      <ul class="border-t-score border-navy">
        {
          chooser.map((row) => (
            <li class="grid gap-s3 border-b-hairline border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:items-baseline md:gap-s6">
              <p class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">{row.when}</p>
              <p
                class:list={[
                  'font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display',
                  row.none ? 'text-inkMuted' : 'text-ink',
                ]}
              >
                {row.answer}
              </p>
              <p class="max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{row.why}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 3. MONTHLY — a card comparison, because a subscription compares as a card. */}
  <section class="bg-greige">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={2}>Monthly membership</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-inkBody">
        Available at both venues. Two hours of bay time a day, every day, plus the booking window that gets you the
        Saturday slot before anyone else asks for it.
      </p>

      <ul class="mt-s7 grid gap-s6 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          monthly.map((tier) => (
            <li
              class:list={[
                'flex flex-col bg-white p-cell',
                tier.data.recommended ? 'border-t-score border-ember' : 'border-t-hairline border-navy',
              ]}
            >
              <h3 class="font-display text-card leading-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">
                {tier.data.name}
              </h3>

              <p class="mt-s4 flex items-baseline gap-s3">
                <span class="scoreboard text-score-xl leading-score text-ink">${tier.data.price}</span>
                <span class="text-small leading-body text-inkMuted">{tier.data.cadence}</span>
              </p>

              {/* The recommendation is a REASON, not a sticker. */}
              {tier.data.recommended && tier.data.recommendedNote && (
                <p class="mt-s4 border-l-slab border-ember pl-s4 text-small leading-body text-inkBody">
                  {/* One expression, not `$` + a line break + the number: JSX keeps
                    that newline as a space and the page rendered "$ 299". */}
                  <span class="font-display font-bold tracking-display text-ink">{tier.data.recommendedNote}</span>
                  {` — $${tier.data.price} ÷ $${WALK_UP} means it pays for itself past about ${paybackFor(
                    tier.data.price ?? 0,
                  )} hours of bay time a month. Fewer than that and you are better off booking by the hour.`}
                </p>
              )}

              {/* The window is the difference between these tiers and the
                  only reason three of them are cheaper than the fourth, so it
                  is printed with the price rather than left in the list. */}
              {tier.data.window && <p class="caps-label mt-s3 text-label-sm text-inkMuted">{tier.data.window}</p>}

              <p class="mt-s5 text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{tier.data.forWho}</p>

              <ul class="mt-s5 flex-1 border-t-hairline border-navy">
                {tier.data.includes.map((line) => (
                  <li class="border-b-hairline border-navy py-s3 text-small leading-body text-inkBody">{line}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-s7 flex flex-wrap gap-s5">
        <a
          href={globalData.external.membershipsLakeville}
          class={buttonClasses('md', 'primary')}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="membership:lakeville"
        >
          Join at Lakeville <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens the Whoosh store in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href={globalData.external.membershipsStillwater}
          class={buttonClasses('md', 'outline')}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="membership:stillwater"
        >
          Join at Stillwater <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens the Whoosh store in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      {
        /* The winter gap, stated where a buyer meets the summer price rather
          than in a footnote. Untinted `quoted` would be wrong here: nobody is
          holding a winter number back, it genuinely does not exist yet.

          On a WHITE slab, because this band is greige and a `notSet` cell tints
          itself greige — on the alternating field the tint is the same colour as
          the ground, so the mark loses the very form that distinguishes it from
          a `quoted` one. See the ground note in `GapCell`. */
      }
      <div class="mt-s7 max-w-prose-page bg-white p-cell">
        <GapCell
          label="Winter membership"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="These are the summer terms, renewing until 3 October 2026. Winter pricing, included hours and start date have not been set — and winter is this venue's real season."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    /* 4. LINKSFLEX — the fuel gauge. No peer in the competitive scan offers
      prepaid hours with no expiry date; it is the strongest differentiator on the
      site and currently lives in a terms-and-conditions page (strategy.md §2). */
  }
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={3}>LinksFlex — prepaid hours</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-inkBody">
        Buy a block of hours up front and use them whenever. There is no expiry date on them, so a bad month costs you
        nothing, and there is no monthly bill. The one condition is in{' '}
        <a
          href="#before-you-join"
          class="font-bold underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-fast ease-standard hover:text-ember"
          >the small print</a
        > below.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-s5 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-s6 gap-y-s3">
        <ReadoutCell label="Where" size="name">Both venues</ReadoutCell>
        <ReadoutCell label="Also included" size="name">21-day booking window · 10% off food</ReadoutCell>
      </div>

      <FuelGauge
        class="mt-s7"
        walkUp={WALK_UP}
        rows={flex.map((f) => ({
          name: f.data.name,
          window: f.data.window,
          recommended: f.data.recommended,
          recommendedNote: f.data.recommendedNote,
          banks: f.data.banks,
        }))}
      />

      <div class="mt-s7 flex flex-wrap gap-s5">
        <a
          href={globalData.external.membershipsLakeville}
          class={buttonClasses('md', 'primary')}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="linksflex:lakeville"
        >
          Buy a LinksFlex block at Lakeville <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens the Whoosh store in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
        <a
          href={globalData.external.membershipsStillwater}
          class={buttonClasses('md', 'outline')}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          data-analytics="linksflex:stillwater"
        >
          Buy a LinksFlex block at Stillwater <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span class="sr-only">(opens the Whoosh store in a new tab)</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <StubNote
        class="mt-s6"
        needs="The Off-Peak and Senior / Vet windows open at 8am and the Junior window at 2pm, and these are the 2026/27 SEASON prices — Lakeville's winter hours are 8am-10pm, so they agree from the start of winter. They do NOT agree today: the published summer hours run 11am-9pm until 3 October, so an 8am off-peak slot cannot be booked yet. Confirm the date the season pricing takes effect, and whether these windows apply before winter hours begin."
      />
      <StubNote
        class="mt-s5"
        needs="The poster gives two different Sunday windows for Off-Peak: the MONTHLY tier reads 'Sun 5p-10p' and the HOUR PACKAGE reads 'Sun after 3p'. Both are on the page as given, because they may genuinely differ between the two products. Confirm - if they are meant to match, one of them is wrong on the poster and on this page."
      />
      <StubNote
        class="mt-s5"
        needs="Senior / Vet has no eligibility stated anywhere: no qualifying age for senior, and nothing on what counts as a veteran or what proof is wanted. A reduced rate with no published test is a conversation at the till. Get the rule and it becomes a line in the card."
      />
      <StubNote
        class="mt-s5"
        needs="The poster's 'Save 35%' and 'Save 54%' badges are NOT on this page. Against the published $35 walk-up rate the numbers do not come out: Off-Peak works out at $29.15-$33.25 an hour (17-5% off) and Anytime at $39.56-$45.75, which is MORE than walking in. They only make sense against a winter hourly rate, and no winter rate has ever been published - it is still the oldest open gap on the site. Publish the winter rate and the badges can go up with a divisor a customer can check."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* 5. THE SMALL PRINT the playbook requires, in plain words. */}
  <section class="bg-greige" id="before-you-join">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead index={4}>Before you join</SectionHead>
      <dl class="border-t-score border-navy">
        {
          smallPrint.map(([q, a]) => (
            <div class="grid gap-s3 border-b-hairline border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:gap-s6">
              <dt class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">{q}</dt>
              <dd class="max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{a}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }

        {
          /* Guests: RESOLVED 2026-08-04 (client-answers.md §13). This carried a
            PendingTag because the client's own price card said "only available
            for the package purchaser" and "No Guest Fees" in the same breath.
            The answer is yes — members bring guests, and the member has to be
            there. It gets stated plainly because this is the one that costs
            somebody money at the till. */
        }
        <div
          class="grid gap-s3 border-b-hairline border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:gap-s6"
        >
          <dt class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">Guests</dt>
          <dd class="max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">
            Bring them. There is no guest fee on any membership — the only rule is that you have to be there too, since
            the membership is yours rather than the bay's.
          </dd>
        </div>

        {/* Cancellation: nobody has told us the mechanism. That is an absence. */}
        <div class="grid gap-s3 border-b-score border-navy py-row md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] md:gap-s6">
          <dt class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">How to cancel</dt>
          <dd class="max-w-prose-page">
            <GapCell
              label="Notice period and mechanism"
              state="notSet"
              size="text"
              reason="“Automatic monthly renewal until cancelled” is the only language that exists today, and it does not tell anyone how to cancel. We have asked."
            />
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
  <section class="on-dark bg-midnight">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg lg:py-section-lg">
      <SectionHead tone="dark">Not sure yet?</SectionHead>
      <p class="max-w-prose-page text-lead leading-body text-paper">
        Book an hour at the normal rate first. Three hours in a month costs ${WALK_UP * 3}, so a membership only starts
        paying for itself past about {payback} hours — ${cheapestMonthly} ÷ ${WALK_UP}. Buy nothing until then.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-s6"><BookButton size="lg" variant="onDark" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
